<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Red Guards (China)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1966–1968</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Red Guards were militant student and youth groups mobilised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a> at the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cultural-revolution">Cultural Revolution</a> in 1966. They attacked teachers, party officials and 'old' culture, destroying temples, books and artefacts, and soon fought among themselves. From 1968 the army restored order and millions of young people were sent to the countryside.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/red-guards-china.jpg" alt="Red Guards (China)" width="320" height="189" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_Guards_Armband_Calligraphy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
